          or :math:`(C, \text{output\_size}[0], \text{output\_size}[1], \dots)` as described above

    Examples::

        >>> fold = nn.Fold(output_size=(4, 5), kernel_size=(2, 2))
        >>> input = torch.randn(1, 3 * 2 * 2, 12)
        >>> output = fold(input)
        >>> output.size()
